  {
    "@id": "https://persephonetheatre.org/event/the-romeo-initiative-7/#event",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Recommended Audience: 12+ Running time: Approximately 2 hours and 25 minutes, including intermission The perfect man. The perfect romance. Single men are hard to come by in Cold War Germany so when Karin Maynard meets the handsome and attentive Markus Richter while on vacation abroad, it has to be fate. Or is it? Based on a real program in East Germany in which men were trained by the Stasi to be the “perfect man” to woo West German secretaries, The Romeo Initiative is half romantic comedy and half spy thriller with a tantalizing twist. “This play has something for everyone – it is romance, intrigue, spy thriller, and true history all rolled into one fascinating story. The premise feels fantastical and yet it is inspired by true events. I love Trina’s writing, and her work on this play is exceptional. This play will surprise you in all the best ways!” – Heather Cant Featuring: Kristi Frank, Mackenzie Dawson, Jenna “JB” Berenbaum Creative Team: Trina Davies – Playwright Jonathan Seinen – Director Xander Scribante – Assistant Director Hanne Loosen – Set and Costume Designer Judith Schulz – Lighting Designer Jordan Perry – Sound Designer Rachel Walliser – Intimacy Director Ricardo Alvarado – Stage Manager Katie Blackburn-Dust – Assistant Stage Manager Nathaniel Morin – Apprentice Stage Manager"
      }
    ],
