        "@value": "Recommended Audience: 8+ Running time: 2 hours, plus intermission It’s 1938 in Hohman, Indiana, and little Ralphie Parker wants just one thing for Christmas – a shiny new Red Ryder BB gun. But his mother, his teacher, and even Santa Claus insist, “You’ll shoot your eye out!” Rebuffed at every turn, Ralphie schemes to achieve his ultimate desire in time for Christmas. Based on the much-loved film, perfectly capturing childhood fantasy and the nostalgia of family Christmases past, A Christmas Story is the perfect gift for the whole family! “I love this play for the way it looks at our nostalgia for childhood. It celebrates family, tradition, and the magic and fantasy of a child’s experience of growing up. This play is a wonderful experience for the whole family that has all those classic moments that has made the film version an evergreen classic.” – Heather Cant, Artistic Director Youth Cast Schedule Adult Cast: Nathan Coppens, Amanda Trapp, Kenn McLeod, Keisha Mowchenko Youth Cast: [REINDEER CAST] Clark Willoughby, Lochlan McLeod, Xavier Negraeff, Luka Lasnier, Avaya Moore, Kyra Jackson, Tirea Parangi. [ELVES CAST] Kade Adams, Tearyan McConnery-Larabie, Jaxon Leschinski, Jakob Thomas, Brielle Alotso, Amelia Kostiuk, Michael Oluwafifehanmi Olufemi Creative Team:  Heather Cant – Director Ken Mackenzie – Set Designer Conor Farrell – Apprentice Set Designer Anna Yaworski – Costume Designer Whittyn Jason – Lighting Designer Cory Dallas Standing – Sound Designer Jordie Richardson – Fight Director Ricardo Alvarado – Stage Manager Shelby Lyn Lowe – Assistant Stage Manager Lauren Griffin – Apprentice Stage Manager Ohad Winkler, Ian Ninnie – Youth Cast Supervisors"
      }
    ],
