  {
    "@id": "https://persephonetheatre.org/event/blithe-spirit-16/#event",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": ""
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "by Noël Coward Recommended Audience: 12+ Running Time: 2 hours and 35 minutes, plus intermission In this uproarious comedy by the master of wit, socialite and novelist Charles has invited the eccentric medium, Madame Arcati, to his house as research for his next book. But when their dinner-party-turned-séance proves successful, Charles’ marriage is suddenly in jeopardy as he is haunted by the ghost of his first wife. While Charles schemes to get rid of the ghost, she is hard at work trying to get rid of his new wife! One husband and two feuding wives unveils a whole lot of laughs in this mystical comedy of manners! “Noël Coward is a legendary playwright in the classic Western theatre canon so it may surprise audiences that this will mark the first time one of his plays has ever been done by Persephone in our 50-year history. Coward is known as the “Master of Wit” and Blithe Spirit is one of his best. You can expect a sharp, witty comedy with a supernatural twist!” – Heather Cant, Artistic Director Featuring: Johanna Arnott, Shannon Blanchet, Tim Bratton, Kevin Williamson, Lisa Bayliss, Katie Moore, Vanessa Leticia Jetté Director: Skye Brandon Assistant Director: Elizabeth Whitbread Set Designer: Jody Longworth Costume Designer: Miranda Hughes-McKnight Apprentice Costume Designer: Emily Rempel Lighting Designer: Byron Hnatuk Sound Designer: Oli Guselle Stage Manager: Avery Fehr Assistant Stage Manager: Shelby Lyn Lowe Apprentice Stage Manager: Lauren Griffin Dialect Coach: Alison Deon"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://persephonetheatre.org/shows/play/blithe-spirit/"
      }
